SUMMARY: Duplicate Advisory: OpenClaw's device removal and token revocation do not terminate active WebSocket sessions
DETAILS: ### Duplicate Advisory
This advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-2pr2-hcv6-7gwv. This link is maintained to preserve external references.

### Original Description
OpenClaw before 2026.3.28 fails to disconnect active WebSocket sessions when devices are removed or tokens are revoked. Attackers with revoked credentials can maintain unauthorized access through existing live sessions until forced reconnection.
